    "turn_text": "even do it. Of course you do. I mean, this nonsense of a warrant, this amendment of a quote unquote warrant requirement, it's not a warrant requirement. It's a secondary warrant requirement. We already have a warrant requirement to do any investigative step that implicates the fourth amendment on a US person. What our colleagues are trying to implement is a secondary warrant requirement that doesn't have to deal with collection of evidence on US persons, but it has to deal with querying Existing lawfully collected law enforcement databases, NCIC, right, checking people's criminal background checks before you execute an arrest warrant, running of license plates, pings off a DOT database, lawfully collected data, a fugitive squad in the U.S. Marshals that want to ping a TSA database to get a flight manifest and figure out which airport they can safely arrest their fugitive. This is law enforcement, right? Law enforcement",
