    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, part of it was a huge part of it was a flaw in the FBI software that had an automatic opt-in where you had a firm really opt out. If you did not want to check a 702 database with part of your normal course of searches, they fixed that and it's cut it down dramatically, obviously. And, you know, that change coupled with the 56 reforms will prevent any of these abuses from happening. And, quite frankly, a lot of people think it's going to already have its chilling effects. Now that they're criminal penalties, that agents are just going to opt, you know, they don't want to put their families or houses at risk, they're just not going to do it. So that's already to be let alone this secondary warrant requirement. We've always had to make this decision in our country on the continuum of 100% privacy, 100% security, where we all fall. And it's all about democracy and this conversation to figure out where we've fallen this continuum. You can't go all in for one or the other, right? That's anarchy and that's dictatorships, right? We've got to figure out as a nation where we want to fall, where we can accomplish and protect both. And I think this build us",
